# Scouting Opponent Players — Locked Three-Column Layout

Canonical commit baseline: `d3694e8` (“Add team scouting workflows”), as amended only by
explicit Scouting layout restorations that preserve this contract.

**Canonical component:** `src/features/scouting/components/ScoutingWorkspace.tsx`
(`OpponentPlayersMasterDetail`). Do not introduce a second Opponent Players main UI.

## Locked desktop contract

On desktop, Opponent Players is **always** three columns:

| Region | Width | Data attribute |
| --- | --- | --- |
| LEFT — Teams | ~230–270px (`minmax(14.5rem,16.5rem)`) | `data-scouting-team-column` (+ `data-scouting-team-nav`) |
| MIDDLE — Players | ~280–340px (`minmax(17.5rem,21rem)`) | `data-scouting-player-column` (+ `data-scouting-player-list`) |
| RIGHT — Reports | flex (`minmax(0,1fr)`) | `data-scouting-report-column` (+ `data-scouting-player-workspace`) |

Desktop shell marker: `data-scouting-desktop-columns` with
`className="grid … max-md:hidden"` — **never** `hidden md:grid` (that anti-pattern blanked
desktop while the toolbar still showed a positive player count).

## Interactions (do not change)

- Team select → updates middle roster, keeps a valid player selection, updates right.
- Middle player select → updates **right only**; does **not** open the Player Card.
- Right column: report previews + green **Open player card** (only path that opens the card).
- Report click → opens Report Card.
- Summary cards + Quick AI live on the Player Card Overview (opened via the green button),
  not as a flat-table replacement of this shell.

## Data must not control layout existence

- The three-column shell **always mounts** for the Opponent Players view.
- Loading / empty / error / no-reports states belong **inside** columns (or a banner),
  never by unmounting `data-scouting-desktop-columns`.
- A positive filtered player count must never appear above a blank desktop workspace.

## Tabs

Peer views use `ModuleSectionTabs` (Practice-style). No `rounded-full` pill tabs for
Opponent Players | Teams | Match Reports | Form Submissions.

## Forbidden regressions

- Replacing Opponent Players with a flat directory `<table>` (Teams tab may keep its table).
- Duplicate Scouting main workspaces outside `ScoutingWorkspace`.
- Gating `OpponentPlayersMasterDetail` behind `!loadError` so columns disappear on failure.
